# What does NOT ship in the .vsix.
#
# An extension is downloaded by everyone who installs it, so the default — everything in the folder —
# is the wrong default. This is an allow-list in reverse: the grammars, the two entry points, the
# manifest and the two documents a marketplace page is built from.

install.mjs
# For whoever publishes it, not for whoever installs it.
build-preview.mjs
build-plugin.mjs
preview.png.stamp
# The picture on the marketplace page is served from GitHub — the marketplace does not resolve a
# relative path in a README — so neither the generator nor the file itself belongs in the download.
PUBLISHING.md
.vscodeignore
node_modules/**
# …except the language-service plugin staged by `build-plugin.mjs`. It is what lets the editor's
# SYNTAX server read a block: that server never opens a tsconfig, so a plugin named there never
# reaches it, and this is the only path `tsserver` resolves a contributed plugin from.
!node_modules/@ramonda/**
**/*.map
**/tsconfig.json
**/*.test.*
preview.png
